Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: report NSS 12.5 MPDU retries to cfg80211

NSS 12.5 supplies retry statistics in a separate peer-sync block. Its
legacy tx.retries field stays zero on the tested IPQ5018 even while the
MPDU retry counters advance. cfg80211 expects cumulative MPDU retries;
accumulate the total MPDU retry count into the existing station counter.
Keep the legacy field for firmware without the 12.5 retry block and do
not sum the two sources or count each retried MPDU only once.

This fixes reporting only. Preserve REO duplicate/window checks and all
raw debugfs counters; retry statistics are not unique IP packet losses.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -186,7 +186,11 @@
 			pstats->tx.tx_ucast_bytes +
 			pstats->tx.tx_bcast_bytes;
 		peer->nss.nss_stats->tx_bytes += tx_bytes;
+#ifdef NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_12_5
+		peer->nss.nss_stats->tx_retries += pstats->retry.tx_mpdu_total_retry_count;
+#else
 		peer->nss.nss_stats->tx_retries += pstats->tx.retries;
+#endif

 		for (j = 0; j < NSS_WIFILI_TQM_RR_MAX; j++)
 			tx_dropped += pstats->tx.dropped.drop_stats[j];
